Jungle cats are often spotted amidst human settlement (and are frequently reported to take chickens). Pocock (1939a) reported that jungle cats in Kashmir occupied "nearly every old building about Srinagar," and recently, in southern India, a breeding pair was found occupying an old building in an urban area, near coconut palm plantations (U. Karanth in Zitt. 1991).

